Report View-The main workspace where you create and arrange visualizations such as charts, tables, cards, and slicers to build interactive reports and dashboards.
Data View-Displays the actual data stored in your tables. It allows you to inspect rows and columns and perform basic data-related operations.
Model View-Shows the relationships between tables in your data model. You can create, edit, and manage relationships between tables here.
Fields Pane-Located on the right side, it lists all available tables, columns, and measures. You use it to select fields and add them to visualizations.
Visualizations Pane-Provides options for selecting and configuring visual types such as bar charts, line charts, pie charts, cards, and tables. It also lets you format the selected visual.
Filters Pane-Allows you to apply filters to individual visuals, an entire report page, or the whole report to control which data is displayed.
